  "notes": "ガム (from English 'gum') refers to chewing gum in Japanese.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ガムを{噛|か}む: to chew gum\n- {風船|ふうせん}ガム: bubble gum\n- ガムテープ: packing tape (duct tape)\n\nNOTE: ガムテープ (gum tape) refers to packing tape or duct tape, not tape made of gum. This is a wasei-eigo (Japanese-made English) term.\n\nRELATED:\n- ゴム: rubber (different word, often confused)",
